WEBVTT

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:14.245
Hatenkou Yugi

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.556
The departure always comes unexpectedly

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:22.027
It is destined to happen like a coincidence

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:27.829
Your evolving fate starts to grind

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.268
Confused by sudden rain

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.706
Stunned by getting rejected and soaked in the rain

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:41.805
Let’s laugh it off: a new path will open for you

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:45.616
What’s the most precious thing

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:49.187
That’s hidden behind meaningless things

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:57.094
You can make miracles happen, so keep smiling

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:00.596
My Heartbreaking Romance

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:04.836
Let’s go wild as you desire

00:01:04.836 --> 00:01:10.138
Have a blast and live it up: that’s my style

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.171
Your Heartrending Sorrow

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.416
| will leave it alone for now

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:24.879
So let’s begin our adventure right here

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:29.992
Am | ever

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:37.001
Do you think you are blessed with friends?

00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:39.196
| would say no.

00:01:39.538 --> 00:01:43.542
| don’t even know why
I’m traveling with these people.

00:01:43.542 --> 00:01:45.510
Are you satisfied with your current situation?

00:01:45.911 --> 00:01:49.312
Nope. Although, | don’t have
any particular complaints.

00:01:49.548 --> 00:01:50.549
Okay, then fet me ask...

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:53.017
is your fife still
"damn boring"?

00:01:53.318 --> 00:01:54.751
No! Hell no!

00:01:55.487 --> 00:02:02.051
As long as you're with me, there’s no way
you’d get bored. I’m 100% positive about that.

00:02:02.227 --> 00:02:05.458
Go ahead and laugh hysterically, you bastards!

00:02:06.765 --> 00:02:09.529
Must you brag when you're in handcuffs?

00:02:10.302 --> 00:02:11.360
Exactly.

00:02:11.703 --> 00:02:14.297
I'd rather have peace and quietness.

00:02:15.173 --> 00:02:21.305
As you can see, this episode of Hatenkou Yugi
will be brought to you from prison.

00:02:22.614 --> 00:02:26.448
Wound of
Thé Scar

00:02:36.028 --> 00:02:36.926
Listen...

00:02:37.362 --> 00:02:41.526
| hate to say this over and over again...

00:02:42.134 --> 00:02:45.729
The guide shouldn't get lost, for God’s sake.

00:02:46.104 --> 00:02:47.571
Be quiet!

00:02:48.006 --> 00:02:51.737
The fact that there’s nothing
where I’m headed to is the problem.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.609
They better start over.

00:02:53.945 --> 00:02:56.743
A town like this should be rebuilt from scratch.

00:02:56.915 --> 00:02:58.507
You sound like a queen.

00:02:58.684 --> 00:02:59.708
Hmph.

00:03:00.285 --> 00:03:02.310
It’s totally Heat-tan’s fault, anyway.

00:03:02.788 --> 00:03:08.283
He just took off hastily, so | have no idea
which inn we’re supposed to meet him at.

00:03:09.828 --> 00:03:13.787
Either way, it doesn’t look like
we're headed in the right direction.

00:03:14.499 --> 00:03:15.557
Really?

00:03:16.068 --> 00:03:20.266
To me, it looks like the perfect place
where Heat-tan might be.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:22.998
Ow...

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:25.472
Are you all right?

00:03:26.111 --> 00:03:28.545
H-help me! Someone’s chasing me!

00:03:29.314 --> 00:03:30.948
If | get caught, they'll kill me.

00:03:30.949 --> 00:03:31.745
Please!

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.312
No, | can’t.

00:03:34.352 --> 00:03:35.284
Just like that?

00:03:35.654 --> 00:03:38.680
An innocent boy is asking for help, you know.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:41.049
How can you be so cruel?

00:03:41.226 --> 00:03:43.561
Demon! Devil! Trashy pig!

00:03:43.562 --> 00:03:45.029
That’s quite a declaration.

00:03:45.797 --> 00:03:48.766
If you’re in trouble, you should go to the police.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.767
Actually, I’m being chased by the police.

00:03:51.937 --> 00:03:54.497
If | get caught, they'll kill me.

00:03:54.973 --> 00:03:57.999
| can’t die before taking revenge for my dad!

00:03:59.377 --> 00:04:00.503
What do you mean?

00:04:00.912 --> 00:04:02.072
You can tell me.

00:04:04.249 --> 00:04:05.910
We found him! Over here!

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.144
Hold it right there!

00:04:12.357 --> 00:04:15.326
So, you succeeded in capturing that kid?

00:04:15.827 --> 00:04:16.691
And?

00:04:19.397 --> 00:04:21.592
Oh? He has helpers?

00:04:21.833 --> 00:04:23.061
Very well.

00:04:23.602 --> 00:04:26.571
It’s going to be quite
an entertaining game this time.

00:04:31.309 --> 00:04:34.904
Well? Anything you want to say to us, Little Boy?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:41.018
I’m sorry, but | don’t know
what to do without someone’s help.

00:04:41.153 --> 00:04:42.677
Concerning revenge?

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.887
Revenge...

00:04:47.826 --> 00:04:50.158
This is the second time | heard
someone else use that word.

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:52.390
| remember the first time...

00:04:53.532 --> 00:04:54.624
Listen, Alzeid...

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.062
you're traveling alone, right?

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:58.165
Then, why don’t you join me?

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.805
| just started on my journey today.

00:05:02.607 --> 00:05:04.507
Are you expecting me to babysit you?

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:05.674
No thanks.

00:05:07.179 --> 00:05:09.841
He claimed that I’d be a burden to him.

00:05:10.849 --> 00:05:13.647
Then, he revealed how he ended up on his journey.

00:05:14.386 --> 00:05:16.877
I’m searching for a woman who killed my father.

00:05:17.389 --> 00:05:19.516
That’s the purpose of my journey.

00:05:20.091 --> 00:05:27.759
When the man died, | lost both
a father figure and a part of myself.

00:05:29.301 --> 00:05:32.930
So, this revenge is actually personal as well.

00:05:33.905 --> 00:05:37.397
It’s as complex as a difficult brain-teaser.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:41.179
| still haven’t figured out what he meant.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:47.943
That said, it isn’t what
keeps me going on my journey.

00:05:49.087 --> 00:05:51.817
| have no interest in revenge.

00:05:53.124 --> 00:05:56.355
It doesn’t matter who’s seeking revenge, either.

00:06:00.232 --> 00:06:03.360
My dad was locked up here, too.

00:06:04.269 --> 00:06:08.205
Since it was a minor offense,
| was told he’d be out soon.

00:06:08.607 --> 00:06:11.007
But no matter how long | waited,
he was never released.

00:06:11.443 --> 00:06:13.775
So | searched for the prison’s supervisor
to ask him in person.

00:06:15.714 --> 00:06:19.309
Oh, that prisoner? He was executed yesterday.

00:06:19.918 --> 00:06:21.283
Why?

00:06:21.486 --> 00:06:24.250
| don’t remember such trivial things.

00:06:25.257 --> 00:06:27.521
What? You want his remains?

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:31.554
Give it a day or two,
and you'll find it in the landfill.

00:06:34.799 --> 00:06:35.663
You brat!

00:06:36.001 --> 00:06:36.831
Catch him!

00:06:37.002 --> 00:06:40.301
I'll make sure he suffers just like his father did!

00:06:41.606 --> 00:06:43.403
And that’s that.

00:06:43.842 --> 00:06:46.140
Man, that’s not nice.

00:06:46.378 --> 00:06:48.846
There’s no way he can get away with that.

00:06:50.982 --> 00:06:53.473
Hey there, Rahzel-chan.

00:06:53.785 --> 00:06:56.420
Heat-tan! What are you doing here?

00:06:56.421 --> 00:06:59.557
You know, when | was looking for lodging,

00:06:59.557 --> 00:07:02.321
someone told me about this nice place
and it includes three daily meals.

00:07:02.427 --> 00:07:03.018
Liar.

00:07:03.795 --> 00:07:06.229
| bet you got ripped off by some sketchy joint,

00:07:06.798 --> 00:07:10.393
and they arrested you
for beating a man half to death.

00:07:10.835 --> 00:07:12.996
How could you speak so ill of people?

00:07:13.405 --> 00:07:16.670
Buying ladies isn’t my thing.

00:07:17.008 --> 00:07:19.636
It’s all about free love.

00:07:20.078 --> 00:07:21.636
You mean, blackmailing?

00:07:22.113 --> 00:07:24.581
But man, you really are a reckless kid.

00:07:24.916 --> 00:07:30.650
You see, this prison is infamous
for not letting their prisoners out once they’re in.

00:07:31.189 --> 00:07:35.319
Nowadays, people don’t like the idea
of having a prison in the city,

00:07:35.794 --> 00:07:42.700
so this prison accepts prisoners
from all over the place while taking a large profit.

00:07:43.001 --> 00:07:44.901
They’re making a fortune.

00:07:45.236 --> 00:07:49.607
But it won't be too long
before this place is completely filled up.

00:07:49.607 --> 00:07:50.938
Help us!

00:07:51.343 --> 00:07:57.680
So they regularly discard prisoners
to create more vacancies.

00:07:58.049 --> 00:08:02.486
N-no way... That’s why they killed Dad?

00:08:04.022 --> 00:08:08.015
When you realize your turn is next,
it’s already too late.

00:08:08.927 --> 00:08:09.916
Here’s your meal.

00:08:10.195 --> 00:08:13.722
Enjoy. It could be your last meal.

00:08:14.165 --> 00:08:17.535
Woo-hoo! Here comes the stinky food!

00:08:17.535 --> 00:08:19.469
| might become addicted to it.

00:08:20.138 --> 00:08:21.400
You want me to help you?

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.705
You’re ready to avenge your dad, right?

00:08:30.582 --> 00:08:31.947
W-wait!

00:08:32.484 --> 00:08:33.678
Just like that?

00:08:36.054 --> 00:08:38.181
Let me finish my meal, at least.

00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:42.392
Damn, what’s going on? How did you...

00:08:43.461 --> 00:08:46.330
Kid, take his gun.

00:08:46.331 --> 00:08:47.525
O-okay.

00:08:47.832 --> 00:08:49.390
N-no way.

00:08:49.501 --> 00:08:51.935
How come your gun wasn’t confiscated?

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.259
| guess it was my charm.

00:08:53.838 --> 00:08:57.274
Just so you know, my cigarette is also safe
thanks to my charm.

00:08:57.475 --> 00:08:58.876
That’s not fair!

00:08:58.877 --> 00:09:02.040
My bear was seized right away!

00:09:04.749 --> 00:09:07.309
What? Those kids escaped?

00:09:07.585 --> 00:09:10.281
All right. Follow the usual procedures.

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:16.486
Well, well, | guess I'll sit back
and enjoy the show.

00:09:17.162 --> 00:09:19.722
Uh-oh, they found us already?

00:09:20.131 --> 00:09:21.765
This is a prison after all.

00:09:21.766 --> 00:09:24.030
I’m sure they have tight security measures.

00:09:24.602 --> 00:09:28.732
Security? You mean traps to capture fugitives,

00:09:29.107 --> 00:09:32.543
like collapsing roofs,
or vicious dogs chasing after you?

00:09:33.745 --> 00:09:35.337
That’s so classic.

00:09:35.814 --> 00:09:39.011
Wait, what was that sound?

00:09:42.454 --> 00:09:43.955
What the heck is that?

00:09:43.955 --> 00:09:45.684
It’s truly classic!

00:09:45.824 --> 00:09:47.155
We gotta run. Hang on!

00:09:47.425 --> 00:09:49.586
Now is my chance, Rahzel-chan!

00:09:50.328 --> 00:09:52.523
Hey! What’s the idea?

00:09:52.964 --> 00:09:53.794
What is that?

00:09:54.299 --> 00:09:58.099
Fine! | don’t mind anymore. Just run!

00:09:58.536 --> 00:09:59.332
You bet!

00:10:09.647 --> 00:10:11.979
This time our guests
seem to be putting on a good show.

00:10:12.517 --> 00:10:16.851
Looks like they’ll manage to keep us entertained
right up to the final stage.

00:10:19.724 --> 00:10:23.194
Dobermans?! How classic can they get?

00:10:23.194 --> 00:10:26.220
Nah, they’re just lame.

00:10:28.733 --> 00:10:30.034
O-okay, now what?

00:10:30.034 --> 00:10:32.025
Look at the enormous iron gate ahead of us.

00:10:32.237 --> 00:10:34.137
Just keep going.

00:10:42.247 --> 00:10:43.373
What’s this place?

00:10:44.182 --> 00:10:45.740
Something is rotten in here.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.614
Uh-oh.

00:10:52.991 --> 00:10:56.085
| wouldn’t normally harm small animals.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.676
Whoa, you’re a beast of a man.

00:11:19.284 --> 00:11:21.411
Men are all wild animal tamers.

00:11:21.986 --> 00:11:25.149
Would you like my cute one to go wild, too?

00:11:27.192 --> 00:11:28.489
As long as | can whip it.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.629
BARAAG!

00:11:33.131 --> 00:11:33.961
What’s wrong?

00:11:37.702 --> 00:11:39.795
This... is my dad’s.

00:11:43.908 --> 00:11:44.840
Wait...

00:11:45.977 --> 00:11:47.205
... does that mean...

00:11:49.614 --> 00:11:51.013
He’s in there?

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:06.693
My dad... Is he really inside there?

00:12:08.099 --> 00:12:09.566
| get it.

00:12:10.068 --> 00:12:14.232
| guess avenging his father
draws attention to your own situation.

00:12:14.872 --> 00:12:16.396
What’s your point?

00:12:17.175 --> 00:12:24.843
Well, | bet it’s easy for you
to deal with someone else’s pain,

00:12:25.316 --> 00:12:26.874
rather than directly facing your own.

00:12:30.288 --> 00:12:32.688
If you're picking a fight, just bring it on.

00:12:33.992 --> 00:12:36.153
Really? You sure?

00:12:36.494 --> 00:12:38.621
You don’t know what you’re getting into.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.196
Are you sure you can handle it, Al-kiddo?

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:46.334
Oh, c’mon! Give it a rest, you idiots!

00:12:46.671 --> 00:12:51.108
Jeez. I’m sure it’s fun to tease Alzeid,
but stop messing with him.

00:12:51.542 --> 00:12:52.910
| know what it feels like, though.

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:53.944
Bummer.

00:12:53.945 --> 00:12:55.344
No whining!

00:12:56.281 --> 00:12:58.442
And let me remind you, Alzeid...

00:12:58.716 --> 00:13:03.915
the reason I’m traveling with you
has nothing to do with your silly revenge.

00:13:09.894 --> 00:13:11.088
Let’s get out of here.

00:13:11.529 --> 00:13:14.698
This isn’t the place you want to be.

00:13:14.699 --> 00:13:18.100
Well, well, | hope you can stay longer.

00:13:18.469 --> 00:13:20.699
The fun is yet to come.

00:13:35.186 --> 00:13:43.355
Ladies and gentlemen, welcome
to the underground arena of Ariamail Prison.

00:13:44.295 --> 00:13:47.560
| am Supervisor Riesfelat.

00:13:48.066 --> 00:13:50.933
Your efforts to come this far
are worthy of my praise.

00:13:51.869 --> 00:13:56.369
However, as long you live,
you must continue to fight.

00:13:58.042 --> 00:14:04.914
And the last man standing will be released;
it’s a “Zero-sum Game.”

00:14:09.187 --> 00:14:11.781
Your father fought well, too.

00:14:12.523 --> 00:14:17.460
He fought desperately when he learned
that his son was coming to visit him every day.

00:14:17.962 --> 00:14:19.293
Dad...

00:14:20.331 --> 00:14:27.100
Now that you understand, it’s time for you
to pay the price for throwing the rock at me.

00:14:27.772 --> 00:14:29.205
Listen up, prisoners!

00:14:29.674 --> 00:14:34.174
In honor of our special guests
today, we shall bend the rules.

00:14:34.712 --> 00:14:36.680
They'll be your targets!

00:14:37.815 --> 00:14:42.218
Now, go ahead and send them to Hell.

00:14:45.123 --> 00:14:46.988
Man, what a drag.

00:14:47.492 --> 00:14:49.858
Really? You don’t find this fun?

00:14:50.094 --> 00:14:51.288
Absolutely not!

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:56.061
Speaking of which, | wonder what Hell is like.

00:15:00.071 --> 00:15:01.939
It’s nice of them to invite us.

00:15:01.939 --> 00:15:03.668
How about we have a picnic lunch?

00:15:06.544 --> 00:15:11.277
Make the omelets sweet for me.
Those fluffy ones.

00:15:13.551 --> 00:15:16.520
Rejected. A sweet omelet is just wrong.

00:15:17.822 --> 00:15:18.789
Huh?

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:24.150
Besides, it doesn’t look like
we'll be departing soon, unfortunately.

00:15:27.231 --> 00:15:28.999
How impressive.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.401
Hey, you three right there.

00:15:30.401 --> 00:15:35.600
If you want to get out of here, take down that kid!

00:15:36.974 --> 00:15:39.602
Shut up, Baldy.

00:15:39.977 --> 00:15:40.841
What?

00:15:42.914 --> 00:15:46.782
Your Baldy-talk
is impossible to decipher, Baldy.

00:15:47.084 --> 00:15:49.780
Go ahead and keep getting balder forever, Baldy.

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:56.151
By the way, | don’t like being looked down on.

00:15:56.694 --> 00:16:00.061
Whoa, Alzeid is being so arrogant.

00:16:00.531 --> 00:16:04.297
Then again, that was a reasonable statement.

00:16:04.735 --> 00:16:07.602
Shall we knock him off his high horse?

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.508
Sure thing!

00:16:18.483 --> 00:16:19.279
What?

00:16:19.617 --> 00:16:21.517
Excuse me, Mister!

00:16:23.988 --> 00:16:25.751
Now, come over here!

00:16:33.097 --> 00:16:36.555
What was that? She has magical powers?

00:16:38.603 --> 00:16:39.399
Don’t move.

00:16:43.107 --> 00:16:44.904
M-my dad...

00:16:46.777 --> 00:16:48.005
This is for my dad!

00:16:49.714 --> 00:16:50.738
Are you sure about that?

00:16:53.451 --> 00:16:56.249
Oops. They caught us.

00:16:56.821 --> 00:17:00.985
Drop your gun if you want to save their lives.

00:17:04.996 --> 00:17:05.894
I-I’m sorry!

00:17:07.999 --> 00:17:12.732
Why is it so hard for Elmier
to understand this situation?

00:17:13.504 --> 00:17:15.597
What about Alzeid?

00:17:17.842 --> 00:17:21.073
As | thought, revenge is a worthless act.

00:17:22.313 --> 00:17:27.148
Elmier, you will never
hit the target trembling like that.

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:32.416
Go on. Raise the gun barrel, and take a good shot.

00:17:32.757 --> 00:17:37.023
The moment you miss,
you'll get riddled with bullets.

00:17:37.295 --> 00:17:38.523
Miss...

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:42.700
Once the bullet scatters
his warm blood and cerebrospinal fluid,

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.759
it will pierce through his skull.

00:17:45.269 --> 00:17:50.366
The vivid image of his dying face
with eyeballs and brain tissue rupturing...

00:17:50.641 --> 00:17:54.042
You'll be haunted by it for the rest of your life.

00:17:54.278 --> 00:17:55.768
Are you prepared for that?

00:17:56.781 --> 00:17:58.715
Q-of course!

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:00.274
I see.

00:18:00.918 --> 00:18:02.786
Okay, suit yourself.

00:18:02.787 --> 00:18:04.482
Wh-what are you doing?

00:18:05.156 --> 00:18:06.384
It’s simple.

00:18:06.857 --> 00:18:09.052
I’m taking revenge, just like you.

00:18:09.493 --> 00:18:13.520
The moment you shoot Baldy,
my friends will be killed.

00:18:14.131 --> 00:18:17.801
So | will take my revenge upon you for them.

00:18:17.802 --> 00:18:18.826
What?

00:18:19.036 --> 00:18:21.038
I’m not the one who’s killing them!

00:18:21.038 --> 00:18:22.266
It’s the same thing.

00:18:22.707 --> 00:18:25.403
They’ll be killed as a consequence of your action.

00:18:25.977 --> 00:18:30.277
| won't forgive anyone who takes away
the people | cherish.

00:18:31.082 --> 00:18:35.178
After | shoot you,
ll exterminate every one of them.

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:40.616
And soon afterwards,
someone else will kill me, too.

00:18:42.627 --> 00:18:44.754
That’s what it means to kill someone.

00:18:45.529 --> 00:18:48.657
Do you have the courage to increase
the never-ending sorrow?

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:54.794
Are you really determined
to inflict your pain on others?

00:18:56.807 --> 00:18:58.365
What’s up with that?

00:18:58.709 --> 00:19:03.305
| mean, so many people died
because of this guy!

00:19:03.748 --> 00:19:05.579
Yeah, but sorry...

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.676
| am sorry.

00:19:08.419 --> 00:19:09.613
They are no longer here.

00:19:09.887 --> 00:19:16.258
Instead of tens or hundreds or thousands
of lives that | didn’t know, | still choose those two.

00:19:32.309 --> 00:19:36.746
Instead of living for the dead,
you must live your life to the fullest.

00:19:37.682 --> 00:19:41.015
Don’t give me that cheerless look.
Show me your smile.

00:19:41.485 --> 00:19:44.545
You look more attractive that way.

00:19:52.663 --> 00:19:54.464
Don’t think we spared your life.

00:19:54.465 --> 00:19:55.261
What?

00:19:55.933 --> 00:20:04.363
Right now, right here, we are going to give you
a beating, more intense than death.

00:20:04.909 --> 00:20:06.171
Enjoy.

00:20:28.933 --> 00:20:31.424
Man, that was so nice to hear.

00:20:32.002 --> 00:20:34.804
Like, "You're important to me" and
"Am | good enough for you?"

00:20:34.805 --> 00:20:36.473
and "I love you," and
"Care to feel my hard embra—"

00:20:36.474 --> 00:20:38.101
Stop fantasizing!

00:20:38.409 --> 00:20:42.646
In any case, revenge is a worthless act, huh?

00:20:42.646 --> 00:20:47.948
Yeah. Whatever the reason is, killing is killing.

00:20:48.352 --> 00:20:56.657
Besides, if you can avoid creating a new wound
on the scar, don’t you think that’s better?

00:20:57.261 --> 00:20:58.694
It’s not your concern.

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:00.488
| guess not.

00:21:01.465 --> 00:21:04.195
But you'd still take revenge for us, wouldn’t you?

00:21:05.536 --> 00:21:07.834
No way. Not gonna happen.

00:21:08.506 --> 00:21:11.600
| mean, we’re prepared
to share the same fate, aren’t we?

00:21:12.743 --> 00:21:16.179
I’m not gonna die,
and I’m not gonna let you die, either.

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:20.214
We'll grow old together and become
tea drinking buddies.

00:21:20.584 --> 00:21:22.686
That'll be a mind-blowing happy life.

00:21:22.686 --> 00:21:26.247
I’m going to become an adorable old lady.

00:21:27.057 --> 00:21:30.254
So, | hope you become
charming old gentlemen. Both of you.

00:21:33.798 --> 00:21:35.390
You bet!

00:21:43.674 --> 00:21:47.344
As | hear the sound of laughter

00:21:47.344 --> 00:21:50.973
Coming from the room next door

00:21:51.148 --> 00:21:58.350
| slowly wake up to the morning that | adore

00:21:58.722 --> 00:22:05.958
Somewhere | dreamed of a painting

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:13.534
| just painted a new chair for you

00:22:13.704 --> 00:22:18.204
Even if the sorrowful story

00:22:20.644 --> 00:22:29.348
Is lying in wait beyond the curtain

00:22:31.355 --> 00:22:38.591
Even if we may feel like strangers tomorrow

00:22:38.863 --> 00:22:45.996
| believe in the perfect miracle that you'll still be here

00:22:46.303 --> 00:22:53.641
The hand you reached out shows no sign of parting

00:22:53.978 --> 00:23:01.714
As | grow teary-eyed, | just want to hold you now
